{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":1238815,"username":"recuadrala","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.deeplearning.ai/recuadrala/{size}/137331_2.png","created_at":"2026-11-02T18:14:11.054Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eLecture notes for the \u003cstrong\u003eEvaluating \u0026amp; Improving Agentic Applications\u003c/strong\u003e course.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNote:\u003c/strong\u003e These slides haven’t been maintained, and you might find missing topics and incorrect information in them, as opposed to lecture videos, where we try to update the misinformation or errors as soon as we are aware of them. \u003cstrong\u003eWe encourage you to make your own notes.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModule 1: Foundations of Evals\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/c8xBrMPWqkILoU6CWXklx4kFs8Z.pdf\"\u003eM1-Evals.pdf\u003c/a\u003e (3.8 MB)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModule 2: Observing and Benchmarking Agents\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/9wgIKm0rLjWcOnUJdsVphq2ms98.pdf\"\u003eM2-Evals.pdf\u003c/a\u003e (3.6 MB)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModule 3: Building Evaluators You Can Trust\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/tLSAIa9bPtyFDEq1AqLAkqDmyfR.pdf\"\u003eM3-Evals.pdf\u003c/a\u003e (5.9 MB)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModule 4: Evaluating Agent Actions and Outcomes\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/6g4jtQ0QNcMsyIOESETOiLUWS1m.pdf\"\u003eM4-Evals.pdf\u003c/a\u003e (1.8 MB)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eModule 5: Improving Agentic Applications\u003c/s